{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/pulls/1175","id":4959221947,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUoK9js8AAAABJ5e4uw","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/pull/1175","diff_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/pull/1175.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/pull/1175.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/issues/1175","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/pulls/1175/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/pulls/1175/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/issues/1175/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/statuses/8f5127d4feebcaa63a0bc0c751dc4a1c1e7dd8d3","number":1175,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Place reconstructed Otis Bardwell beside the Wolf Point wagons","user":{"login":"kevinrhaas","id":4193586,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTM1ODY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4193586?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Adds the first reconstructed standing resident beside the Wolf Point wagons using the repaired Bardwell & Otis portable model. Connected waistcoat shoulders, grounded shoes and identity cards distinguish reconstructed appearance and placement from the historically modelled firm.\n\nCanonical authoring/export remains source `96c4da4b` and successful run `39736567239`. The eight Bardwell raw/web GLBs, placement, person data and human runtime are unchanged by the final test repairs and DEV integration. Photographic finishing, complete tailoring, other people/eras, walking, drivers and riders remain open under T-1789.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Authored source `248ecfb56` passed full preflight: 1,048 checks including 381 self-tests, committed-HEAD checks and postcommit publication/mirror parity.\n- All four repaired published snapshot cells passed on immutable `248ecfb56`: desktop/mobile stages 1–2 each 194 passed/0 failed; desktop/mobile stages 9–12 each 69 passed/0 failed. The repairs retain exact census comparisons and the actual visible glossary meaning/viewport/dismiss assertions. Original `fe98` batch failures remain failures; these results do not claim a full current-head batch.\n- Existing CI integration run `39861691808` succeeded and pushed `8f5127d4feebcaa63a0bc0c751dc4a1c1e7dd8d3`, tree `deb88944d9898183b391a03376de8bb28a2a91a3`, direct parents `248ecfb56` and DEV `bbe4de604`. Actual incoming paths exactly match the DEV delta: Kimball/First Presbyterian geometry, 1904 context and associated provenance; the person runtime, assets, 1835 scene and smoke source are unchanged.\n- Current integration normal CI, fresh published stages 14/15 in both viewports and focused original What's-new/QA-11 in both viewports remain pending. Historical valid cells retain their original source labels; current checks cover the changed geometry, context, global liberties and release feed.\n- Earlier person desktop/mobile images and documented supplemental timing failures retain their original scope. No photographic completion or broad parent-ticket closure.\n\nDEV only. Source, evidence, claims and recovery instructions are periodically committed and pushed to `kevinrhaas/chicago-tickets`.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-21T22:29:26Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T22:38:47Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"kevinrhaas:steward/1835-workwear-repair-20261021","ref":"steward/1835-workwear-repair-20261021","repo":{"id":1384299918,"node_id":"R_kgDOUoK9jg","name":"chicago","full_name":"kevinrhaas/chicago","owner":{"login":"kevinrhaas","id":4193586,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTM1ODY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4193586?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":null,"homepage":null,"language":"Python","visibility":"public","is_template":false,"topics":[],"forks_count":0,"forks":0,"stargazers_count":0,"watchers_count":0,"watchers":0,"open_issues_count":7,"open_issues":7,"size":11675108,"default_branch":"main","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":true,"h